# The shared vectors and the recorded fixtures are read byte for byte (their
# sha256 is pinned in the tests that load them; a vector is never edited to
# make a test pass). No line-ending conversion on any checkout: #146's whole-
# suite run on Windows found hkdf_wycheproof red on CRLF bytes alone.
tests/vectors/** -text
tests/fixtures/** -text
fuzz/corpus/** -text
# The BIP-39 wordlists are parsed at compile time, one word per LF-terminated
# line; a CRLF checkout would put a CR in every word (the parser refuses it)
# and move each file's pinned sha256 (#89).
src/compat/bip39/wordlists/*.txt -text
# The certificate collation table is parsed at compile time, one DUCET row per
# LF-terminated line; a CRLF checkout puts a CR in every line and the parser
# refuses it (#249, the same rule as the wordlists).
src/auth/certificates/collation_latin1.txt -text
